--TEST--
`Core\Response::slotted()` called from a `Core\Html::later` slot throws `LogicError`, because the main script has ended, and the page is still sent whole -- `rule:core-classes/html-later`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The program sends a request to itself. `Core\Test::request` runs this file
// again for it, and in that run the first branch is the page.
if (Core\Env::context() == Core\Env::Context::Request) {
    // The checker cannot see into `$slotted`, so the call compiles. The slot
    // runs after the main script, so the call throws `LogicError`.
    var $slotted = fn(): void => { Core\Response::slotted(); };
    echo Core\Html::later(fn(): void => {
        try {
            $slotted();
        } catch (LogicError $e) {
            echo $e->message;
        }
    });
} else {
    var $page = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/blog");
    echo $page->status(), "\n";
    echo $page->body(), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
200
`Core\Response::slotted()` was called after the main script ended. Call it before the main script returns.
